{"type":"FeatureCollection","features":[{"type":"Feature","properties":{"place":"bhutan-china-north","region":"BT","donors":"CN;rule/cn-tibet","rank":3,"whose_line":"OpenStreetMap mappers: the Bhutan-controlled part of the northern Bhutan–China disputed area ('Bhutan Actually Control Baiyu Area')","publisher":"OpenStreetMap contributors","source_url":"https://www.openstreetmap.org/relation/11789426","version_or_date":"snapshot 2026-10-04T06:57:51Z (Overpass attic query); relation 11789426 v32 (2026-06-23T12:42:13Z)","feature_id":"relation 11789426","licence":"ODbL 1.0","notes":"Contradiction: Natural Earth's 'Bhutan (northwest valleys)' (1,237 km², 89.8–90.6°E) lies where DoS has China (1,227 km²) and overlaps none of OSM's Bhutan–China disputed areas. This file takes OSM's polygon for Bhutan-held disputed land in the north (claimed_by CN, controlled_by BT; part of 'Beyul'). That it is the register's Pasamlung/Jakarlung is not verified. It lies wholly in GADM's Bhutan, so it moves no land: the 1,220 km² of Tibet that Natural Earth's polygon gave to BT stay with Tibet.","input_sha256":"1838423be70b3ca5632ef5eaec9e63dbcc02882905378bd38723d4f9e6125ed7","operation":"assembled from the OSM element's member ways (outer minus inner)","crs":"WGS84 longitude/latitude, as in the source (no reprojection)","source_features":[{"id":"relation 11789426 v32","osm":"relation/11789426","version":32,"timestamp":"2026-06-23T12:42:13Z","name":"Bhutan Actually Control Baiyu Area 不丹实控白玉地区","name:en":"Bhutan Actually Control Baiyu Area","boundary":"disputed","claimed_by":"CN","controlled_by":"BT"}]},"geometry":{"type":"Polygon","coordinates":[[[91.043488,27.8764904],[91.0456044,27.8748581],[91.0482961,27.8745756],[91.049816,27.8739917],[91.050931,27.8743621],[91.0542974,27.8732446],[91.0550573,27.8732258],[91.0553911,27.8729307],[91.056009,27.8729998],[91.0573229,27.8725917],[91.0584024,27.872937],[91.0593399,27.8734455],[91.0603058,27.8729558],[91.0616978,27.8721271],[91.0629336,27.872058